- Adding "node" refinement. A new "node" type shall be instantiated for each physical definition. Such node type represents the type of the vertex associated to a device within the graph of all the interconnected devices of the system. Such type is supposed to be inferred from the keywords used in the physical definition, however, it can be refined by using a JSON specification file to check that the model is relevant according to the device used, or to instantiate context variables, infer channel names, type restrict sensor/actuator inputs/outputs. The syntax for such "node" refinement is as follow (same writing convention as earlier):
```chips

node <physicalFunctionName> implemented by "<JSON_Specification_file_path>" {
    [[having "<JSON_channel_name>" as <physicalChannelName>]
     [having "<JSON_sensor_name>" as <physicalSensorName>]
     [having "<JSON_actuator_name>" as <physicalActuatorName>]
     [having "<JSON_attribute_name>" as <physicalCtxVariableName>]]*
}
```

- Defining how to specify elements of JSON specification files.

- Correct Chips Meta langage according to these modifications (.ecore model and ChipsClassDiagram)